WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.674
Hi! Pronouns stand in for nouns so sentences don't repeat. Today we'll learn subject and object pronouns, and the relative pronouns who, whom, whose and which.

2
00:00:13.824 --> 00:00:26.010
Pronouns have two jobs. The one doing the action is the subject: I, he, she, we, they. The one receiving the action is the object: me, him, her, us, them.

3
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.642
She helped me. She does the helping, and me receives it.

4
00:00:30.792 --> 00:00:39.306
After a preposition, use an object pronoun. So it's between you and me, not between you and I.

5
00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:48.978
Relative pronouns join two ideas into one sentence. Who is for a person doing the action. The boy who won the race is my cousin.

6
00:00:49.128 --> 00:00:58.506
Whom is also for a person, but one who receives the action. The lady whom we met is a doctor. We met her, so she receives the action.

7
00:00:58.656 --> 00:01:05.226
Whose means belonging to someone. The girl whose bag was lost cried. It was her bag.

8
00:01:05.376 --> 00:01:11.490
Which is for things or animals. The book which I borrowed is fun.

9
00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.314
Can't decide between who and whom? Try swapping in he or him.

10
00:01:16.464 --> 00:01:20.754
If he fits, use who. If him fits, use whom.

11
00:01:20.904 --> 00:01:26.778
For example, The man ___ I thanked. We say I thanked him, so the answer is whom.

12
00:01:26.928 --> 00:01:33.258
The man ___ helped me. We say he helped me, so the answer is who.

13
00:01:33.408 --> 00:01:39.090
Watch out! The dog who barked all night is mine is marked wrong in exams!

14
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.514
Who is only for people. A dog is an animal, so use which or that.

15
00:01:44.664 --> 00:01:50.946
Remember: people take who or whom; things and animals take which.

16
00:01:51.096 --> 00:02:02.370
Your turn! The man ___ car was stolen called the police. Which relative pronoun fits? Pause and think.

17
00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:09.474
The answer is whose, because it was the man's car that was stolen. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:09.624 --> 00:02:19.266
Another one! The girl ___ I helped thanked me. Who or whom? Pause and think.

19
00:02:19.416 --> 00:02:27.258
The answer is whom, because I helped her. The girl receives the action. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:27.408 --> 00:02:37.074
Last one! Mum gave the cake to Ben and ___. I or me? Pause and think.

21
00:02:37.224 --> 00:02:45.378
The answer is me, because to is a preposition, so we need an object pronoun. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:45.528 --> 00:02:57.858
Remember: who is a person doing the action, whom is a person receiving it, whose shows belonging, and which is for things and animals. After a preposition, use an object pronoun.

23
00:02:58.008 --> 00:03:02.538
Try the he-or-him trick on your next question!

